@using System.Configuration
@{
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<section class="section" style="min-height:60vh;">
    <div class="section-header">
        <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
            <h1 class="section-h2">Cancellation &amp; <span>Refund Policy</span></h1>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="max-width:800px;font-size:14px;color:#444;line-height:1.9;">
        <p style="margin-bottom:16px;"><em>Last updated: October 2026</em></p>

        <p style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            We understand travel plans can change. This policy explains how cancellations, rescheduling and
            refunds are handled for bookings made with Trip Mitra Holidays. Exact charges can vary by package,
            hotel/airline policy and season — the figures below are our standard policy; your confirmed
            itinerary/invoice will state the specific terms applicable to your booking.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin:24px 0 10px;">1. Cancellation by the Traveller</h3>
        <ul style="margin-bottom:16px;padding-left:20px;">
            <li>45+ days before travel: Advance payment is refundable minus a processing fee, subject to the supplier's own cancellation terms.</li>
            <li>30–44 days before travel: 50% of the total package cost is forfeited.</li>
            <li>15–29 days before travel: 75% of the total package cost is forfeited.</li>
            <li>Less than 15 days before travel / no-show: 100% of the total package cost is forfeited.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            Certain components — flight tickets, visa fees, special-event hotels and peak-season bookings — may
            carry stricter, non-refundable terms set by the respective airline/hotel/operator; these will be
            communicated at the time of booking.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin:24px 0 10px;">2. Rescheduling</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            Requests to reschedule travel dates are subject to availability and may incur a rescheduling fee.
            Where the underlying airline or hotel booking is non-changeable, standard cancellation charges will
            apply instead.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin:24px 0 10px;">3. Cancellation by Trip Mitra Holidays</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            If we are unable to operate a confirmed package due to circumstances beyond our control (force
            majeure, government restrictions, insufficient group size for group tours, etc.), we will offer an
            alternative date/package or a full refund of amounts paid, at the traveller's choice.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin:24px 0 10px;">4. Refund Processing</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            Approved refunds are processed to the original mode of payment within 7–14 business days, subject to
            the refund timelines of our banking and travel-supplier partners.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin:24px 0 10px;">5. How to Cancel</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:32px;">
            To cancel or reschedule a booking, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:@ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["CompanyEmail"]">@ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["CompanyEmail"]</a> or call
            <a href="tel:@ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["CompanyPhoneE164"]">@ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["CompanyPhoneDisplay"]</a> /
            <a href="tel:@ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["CompanyPhoneSecondaryE164"]">@ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["CompanyPhoneSecondaryDisplay"]</a>,
            quoting your booking reference.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
